2026-11-01T19:39:58.4673397Z [36;1m# Note: There is currently no way to distinguish between undefined variables and empty strings in GitHub Actions.[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4673839Z [36;1m# This limitation affects how we handle default values and empty inputs.[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4674194Z [36;1m# For more information, see: https://github.com/actions/runner/issues/924[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4674441Z [36;1m[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4674672Z [36;1m# The following logic implements the configuration priority described in the README:[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4674946Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4675050Z [36;1m# Inputs[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4675170Z [36;1m# Environment Variables[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4675317Z [36;1m# Config File[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4675443Z [36;1m# Defaults[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4675557Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4675828Z [36;1m# As noted above defaults are awkward to handle as GitHub Actions will inject those values as the input[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4684235Z [36;1m# if the caller doesn't provide them, thus if the input matches the default we don't set it as we[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4684847Z [36;1m# can't tell the difference.  Plus if we did set it when it was the default value then it could potentially[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4685357Z [36;1m# override an external environment variable, or something in the callers configuration file, which then wouldn't[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4685757Z [36;1m# match the configuration priority that is documented.[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4685974Z [36;1mset_env_var_if_provided() {[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4686136Z [36;1m  local var_name="$1"[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4686286Z [36;1m  local input_value="$2"[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4686445Z [36;1m  local default_value="$3"[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4686586Z [36;1m[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4686769Z [36;1m  if [ -n "$input_value" ] && [ "$input_value" != "$default_value" ]; then[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4687090Z [36;1m    # If action was provided with explicit input by the caller set that[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4687435Z [36;1m    # Use printf %q to safely escape special characters and prevent command injection[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4687785Z [36;1m    printf 'export %s=%q\n' "$var_name" "$input_value" >> trivy_envs.txt[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4688018Z [36;1m  fi[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4688122Z [36;1m}[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4688221Z [36;1m[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4688393Z [36;1m# Set environment variables, handling those with default values[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4688884Z [36;1m# cf. https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/#environment-variables[0m
2026-11-01T19:39:58.4689242Z [36;1mset_env_var_if_provided "TRIVY_INPUT" "$INPUT_INPUT" ""[0m
